01:15:00,626 --> 01:15:02,366
You want stars?

1051
01:15:02,367 --> 01:15:04,890
I got a skyful

1052
01:15:04,891 --> 01:15:08,241
Put a quarter in the slot
You'll get an eyeful

1053
01:15:08,242 --> 01:15:11,418
You want the moon?
I got her, too

1054
01:15:11,419 --> 01:15:16,902
She's right here waiting
In my pay-per-view

1055
01:15:16,903 --> 01:15:18,382
How long's it been?

1056
01:15:18,383 --> 01:15:22,386
A little moonshine Ain't no sin

1057
01:15:22,387 --> 01:15:25,345
Tell my husband To take his time

1058
01:15:25,346 --> 01:15:31,048
What the boss don't know
The boss won't mind

1059
01:15:42,276 --> 01:15:43,320
Ha!

1060
01:16:12,698 --> 01:16:15,221
-The deal is signed.
-Yes.

1061
01:16:15,222 --> 01:16:17,702
-About time.
-Get on the line.

1062
01:16:17,703 --> 01:16:20,314
I did what I had to do.

1063
01:16:20,924 --> 01:16:22,968
That's what they did too.

1064
01:16:22,969 --> 01:16:26,406
Now, in Hadestown
There were a lot of souls

1065
01:16:26,407 --> 01:16:28,974
Oh, keep your head
Keep your head

1066
01:16:28,975 --> 01:16:31,716
Working on the wall
With all their might

1067
01:16:31,717 --> 01:16:34,763
Huh, kkh!
Oh, you gotta keep your head

1068
01:16:34,764 --> 01:16:37,374
Ya see, they kept
Their heads down low

1069
01:16:37,375 --> 01:16:40,072
Huh, kkh!
If you wanna keep your head

1070
01:16:40,073 --> 01:16:42,988
You couldn't quite
See their faces, right

1071
01:16:42,989 --> 01:16:45,512
But you can hear Them singing

1072
01:16:45,513 --> 01:16:48,211
Oh, keep your head
Keep your head

1073
01:16:48,212 --> 01:16:51,040
Swinging their hammers
In the cold hard ground

1074
01:16:51,041 --> 01:16:53,825
You can hear the sound
Of the pickax ringing

1075
01:16:53,826 --> 01:16:56,393
Huh, kkh!
If you want to keep your head

1076
01:16:56,394 --> 01:17:00,179
And they called it "freedom"

1077
01:17:00,180 --> 01:17:01,878
I'm Eurydice.

1078
01:17:03,314 --> 01:17:04,836
Doesn't anybody hear me?

1079
01:17:04,837 --> 01:17:07,709
-They can hear.
-But they don't care.

1080
01:17:07,710 --> 01:17:10,581
No one has a name down here.

1081
01:17:10,582 --> 01:17:12,844
Mister Hades set you free

1082
01:17:12,845 --> 01:17:15,891
To work yourself Into the ground

1083
01:17:15,892 --> 01:17:18,067
Free to spend eternity

1084
01:17:18,068 --> 01:17:20,939
- In the factory
- And the warehouse

1085
01:17:20,940 --> 01:17:22,375
Where the whistles scream

1086
01:17:22,376 --> 01:17:23,899
And the foremen shout

1087
01:17:23,900 --> 01:17:26,466
- And you're punching in
- And punching in

1088
01:17:26,467 --> 01:17:27,946
And punching in

1089
01:17:27,947 --> 01:17:29,905
And you can't punch out

1090
01:17:29,906 --> 01:17:32,690
And you're way down Hadestown

1091
01:17:32,691 --> 01:17:38,348
Way down, Hadestown

1092
01:17:38,349 --> 01:17:41,091
Way down under the ground

1093
01:17:41,657 --> 01:17:43,701
Why won't anybody look at me?

1094
01:17:43,702 --> 01:17:46,269
-They can look.
-But they don't see.

1095
01:17:46,270 --> 01:17:49,446
-You see?
-It's easier that way.

1096
01:17:49,447 --> 01:17:51,883
Your eyes will look
like that someday.

1097
01:17:51,884 --> 01:17:54,843
Down in the river of oblivion

1098
01:17:54,844 --> 01:17:57,759
You kiss your life goodbye

1099
01:17:57,760 --> 01:17:59,891
And Hades laid His hands on you

1100
01:17:59,892 --> 01:18:03,112
And gave you everlasting life

1101
01:18:03,113 --> 01:18:05,680
And everlasting overtime

1102
01:18:05,681 --> 01:18:07,072
- In the mine
- In the mill

1103
01:18:07,073 --> 01:18:08,595
In the machinery

1104
01:18:08,596 --> 01:18:11,468
Your place On the assembly line

1105
01:18:11,469 --> 01:18:14,384
Replaces all your memories

1106
01:18:14,385 --> 01:18:22,385
Way down, Hadestown

1107
01:18:22,654 --> 01:18:25,917
Way down under the ground

1108
01:18:25,918 --> 01:18:28,354
What do you mean
I'll look like that?

1109
01:18:28,355 --> 01:18:30,966
That's what it
looks like to forget.

1110
01:18:30,967 --> 01:18:33,708
-Forget what?
-Who you are.

1111
01:18:33,709 --> 01:18:36,667
And everything that came before.

1112
01:18:36,668 --> 01:18:38,800
-I have to go!
-Go, where?

1113
01:18:38,801 --> 01:18:42,064
-Go back.
-Oh, and where is that?

1114
01:18:42,065 --> 01:18:45,241
So, what was your name again?

1115
01:18:45,242 --> 01:18:47,635
You've already forgotten.

1116
01:18:48,332 --> 01:18:50,637
You see,
it's like I said before,

1117
01:18:50,638 --> 01:18:53,640
a lot can happen
behind closed doors.

1118
01:18:53,641 --> 01:18:56,208
Eurydice was
a hungry young girl.

1119
01:18:56,209 --> 01:18:58,907
But she wasn't hungry anymore.

1120
01:18:58,908 --> 01:19:02,214
What she was instead was dead.

1121
01:19:02,215 --> 01:19:04,739
Dead to the world anyway.

1122
01:19:04,740 --> 01:19:09,700
You see, she went behind those
doors and signed her life away.

1123
01:19:09,701 --> 01:19:10,875
A-ooh!

1124
01:19:10,876 --> 01:19:14,357
Saw that wheel up in the sky

1125
01:19:14,358 --> 01:19:18,056
-Huh!
-Heard the big bell tolling

1126
01:19:18,057 --> 01:19:19,188
A-ooh!

1127
01:19:19,189 --> 01:19:22,669
A lot of souls have got to die

1128
01:19:22,670 --> 01:19:26,673
To keep the rust belt rolling

1129
01:19:26,674 --> 01:19:30,939
A-ooh!
A lot of spirits gotta break

1130
01:19:30,940 --> 01:19:35,770
To make the Underworld Go round

1131
01:19:35,771 --> 01:19:40,775
Way down, Hadestown

1132
01:19:40,776 --> 01:19:41,950
Huh!

1133
01:19:41,951 --> 01:19:47,042
Way down under the

1134
01:19:47,043 --> 01:19:51,787
Ground

1135
01:20:13,852 --> 01:20:17,508
What I wanted was To fall asleep

1136
01:20:18,857 --> 01:20:22,818
Close my eyes and disappear

1137
01:20:24,254 --> 01:20:27,386
Like a petal on a stream

1138
01:20:27,387 --> 01:20:31,435
A feather on the air

1139
01:20:35,874 --> 01:20:37,049
Lily white

1140
01:20:38,137 --> 01:20:40,139
And poppy red

1141
01:20:40,836 --> 01:20:46,710
I trembled When he laid me out

1142
01:20:46,711 --> 01:20:49,800
"You won't feel a thing" He said

1143
01:20:49,801 --> 01:20:54,675
"When you go down"

1144
01:20:56,895 --> 01:21:01,508
Nothing gonna wake you now

1145
01:21:04,120 --> 01:21:07,645
Now

1146
01:21:18,525 --> 01:21:21,266
Dreams are sweet

1147
01:21:21,267 --> 01:21:22,660
Until they're not

1148
01:21:24,357 --> 01:21:26,881
Men are kind

1149
01:21:26,882 --> 01:21:29,405
Until they aren't

1150
01:21:29,406 --> 01:21:31,320
Flowers bloom

1151
01:21:31,321 --> 01:21:35,586
Until they rot and fall apart

1152
01:21:41,331 --> 01:21:45,725
Is anybody listening?

1153
01:21:45,726 --> 01:21:51,949
I open my mouth
And nothing comes out

1154
01:21:51,950 --> 01:21:56,954
Nothing gonna wake me

1155
01:21:56,955 --> 01:22:01,481
Now

1156
01:22:13,711 --> 01:22:15,321
Flowers

1157
01:22:17,454 --> 01:22:21,936
I remember fields of flowers

1158
01:22:21,937 --> 01:22:25,070
Soft beneath my heels

1159
01:22:26,028 --> 01:22:29,944
Walking in the sun

1160
01:22:29,945 --> 01:22:35,080
I remember someone
Someone by my side

1161
01:22:36,212 --> 01:22:40,302
Turned his face to mine

1162
01:22:40,303 --> 01:22:42,435
And then I turned away

1163
01:22:43,871 --> 01:22:47,788
Into the shade

1164
01:22:59,931 --> 01:23:01,193
You

1165
01:23:04,457 --> 01:23:07,417
The one I left behind

1166
01:23:09,332 --> 01:23:11,987
If you ever walk this way

1167
01:23:12,988 --> 01:23:15,511
Come and find me

1168
01:23:15,512 --> 01:23:18,994
Lying in the bed

1169
01:23:19,995 --> 01:23:23,520
I made

1170
01:23:43,931 --> 01:23:45,281
Come home with me

1171
01:23:46,456 --> 01:23:48,066
-It's you.
-It's me.

1172
01:23:48,762 --> 01:23:49,936
Orpheus

1173
01:23:49,937 --> 01:23:51,069
Eurydice

1174
01:23:52,462 --> 01:23:53,810
I called your name before...

1175
01:23:53,811 --> 01:23:55,160
I know.
You heard?

1176
01:23:55,900 --> 01:23:56,988
No.

1177
01:23:57,336 --> 01:23:59,859
Mister Hermes told me so.

1178
01:23:59,860 --> 01:24:02,253
Whatever happened I'm to blame

1179
01:24:02,254 --> 01:24:03,298
No, no.

1180
01:24:03,299 --> 01:24:04,647
You called my name

1181
01:24:04,648 --> 01:24:06,388
You came

1182
01:24:06,389 --> 01:24:08,520
But how'd you get here?

1183
01:24:08,521 --> 01:24:10,088
On the train?

1184
01:24:11,089 --> 01:24:14,092
No, I walked a long way

1185
01:24:14,919 --> 01:24:16,616
How'd you get beyond the wall?

1186
01:24:18,357 --> 01:24:22,143
I sang a song so beautiful

1187
01:24:22,144 --> 01:24:24,711
The stones wept
And they let me in

1188
01:24:26,322 --> 01:24:28,585
And I can sing us Home again

1189
01:24:29,977 --> 01:24:31,500
No, you can't.

1190
01:24:31,501 --> 01:24:32,763
Yes, I can.

1191
01:24:33,503 --> 01:24:36,027
No, you don't understand.

1192
01:24:36,680 --> 01:24:38,551
Young man!

1193
01:24:43,556 --> 01:24:45,688
I don't think we've met before.

1194
01:24:45,689 --> 01:24:47,429
You're not from
around here, son.

1195
01:24:47,430 --> 01:24:49,213
I don't know
who the hell you are

1196
01:24:49,214 --> 01:24:51,302
but I can tell you don't belong.

1197
01:24:51,303 --> 01:24:53,478
These are working people, son.

1198
01:24:53,479 --> 01:24:55,872
Law-abiding citizens.

1199
01:24:55,873 --> 01:24:58,440
Go back to where you came from.

1200
01:24:58,441 --> 01:25:00,572
You're on the wrong side
of the fence.

1201
01:25:00,573 --> 01:25:02,139
Hades, I know this boy.

1202
01:25:02,140 --> 01:25:03,706
One of the unemployed.

1203
01:25:03,707 --> 01:25:06,056
-His name is Orpheus.
-You stay out of this.

1204
01:25:06,057 --> 01:25:08,624
Orpheus was a poor boy.

1205
01:25:08,625 --> 01:25:09,668
Do you hear me, son?

1206
01:25:09,669 --> 01:25:11,627
You might say he was naive.

1207
01:25:11,628 --> 01:25:13,019
You better run!

1208
01:25:13,020 --> 01:25:15,980
This poor boy
raised up his voice

1209
01:25:16,546 --> 01:25:18,677
with his heart
out on his sleeve.

1210
01:25:18,678 --> 01:25:20,158
No, Orpheus, you should go.

1211
01:25:21,333 --> 01:25:23,856
I'm not going back alone.

1212
01:25:23,857 --> 01:25:25,032
I came to take her home.

1213
01:25:34,129 --> 01:25:36,869
Who the hell
do you think you are?

1214
01:25:36,870 --> 01:25:38,872
Who the hell do you think
you're talking to?

1215
01:25:39,612 --> 01:25:42,658
She couldn't go anywhere
even if she wanted to.

1216
01:25:42,659 --> 01:25:45,051
You are not
from around here, son.

1217
01:25:45,052 --> 01:25:47,097
If you were, then you would know

1218
01:25:47,098 --> 01:25:52,016
that everything and everyone
in Hadestown, I own!

1219
01:25:53,322 --> 01:25:56,629
But I only buy

1220
01:25:57,848 --> 01:25:59,763
what others choose to sell.

1221
01:26:02,766 --> 01:26:04,594
Oh, you didn't know?

1222
01:26:06,161 --> 01:26:08,554
She signed the deal herself.

1223
01:26:09,164 --> 01:26:11,165
- And now she
- It isn't true.

1224
01:26:11,166 --> 01:26:13,515
-belongs to me.
-It isn't true!

1225
01:26:13,516 --> 01:26:14,777
What he said...

1226
01:26:14,778 --> 01:26:16,171
-Eurydice!
-I did!

1227
01:26:16,997 --> 01:26:18,520
I do.

1228
01:26:18,521 --> 01:26:19,652
As for you...

1229
01:26:20,784 --> 01:26:23,089
Everybody gather round!

1230
01:26:23,090 --> 01:26:25,004
Everybody look and see!

1231
01:26:25,005 --> 01:26:29,793
What becomes of trespassers
with no respect for property.

1232
01:27:39,950 --> 01:27:42,908
Why the struggle?
Why the strain?

1233
01:27:42,909 --> 01:27:46,347
Why make trouble?
Why make scenes?

1234
01:27:46,348 --> 01:27:49,741
Why go against the grain?

1235
01:27:49,742 --> 01:27:54,703
Why swim upstream?

1236
01:27:54,704 --> 01:27:57,401
It ain't, it ain't
It ain't no use

1237
01:27:57,402 --> 01:27:59,490
You're bound, you're bound
You're bound to lose

1238
01:27:59,491 --> 01:28:02,276
What's done, what's done
What's done is done

1239
01:28:02,277 --> 01:28:07,281
That's the way the river runs

1240
01:28:07,282 --> 01:28:11,894
So why get wet?
Why break a sweat?

1241
01:28:11,895 --> 01:28:14,897
Why waste your precious breath?

1242
01:28:14,898 --> 01:28:18,727
Why beat your handsome brow?

1243
01:28:18,728 --> 01:28:26,728
Nothing changes

1244
01:28:31,393 --> 01:28:37,049
Anyhow

1245
01:28:56,113 --> 01:28:58,071
If it's true what they say

1246
01:29:00,160 --> 01:29:02,075
If there's nothing to be done

1247
01:29:04,382 --> 01:29:06,428
If it's true that it's too late

1248
01:29:08,386 --> 01:29:10,606
And the girl I love is gone

1249
01:29:12,564 --> 01:29:14,349
If it's true what they say

1250
01:29:16,916 --> 01:29:18,353
Is this how the world is?

1251
01:29:21,921 --> 01:29:23,792
To be beaten and betrayed

1252
01:29:23,793 --> 01:29:26,142
And then be told
That nothing changes

1253
01:29:26,143 --> 01:29:28,406
It'll always be like this

1254
01:29:29,146 --> 01:29:31,888
If it's true what they say

1255
01:29:34,586 --> 01:29:39,243
I'll be on my way

1256
01:29:40,331 --> 01:29:41,331
Huh!

1257
01:29:42,638 --> 01:29:44,639
And the boy turned to go.

1258
01:29:44,640 --> 01:29:45,640
Huh!

1259
01:29:46,206 --> 01:29:48,860
'Cos he thought
no one could hear.

1260
01:29:48,861 --> 01:29:50,079
Huh!

1261
01:29:50,080 --> 01:29:51,646
But everybody knows

1262
01:29:51,647 --> 01:29:53,909
that walls have ears.

1263
01:29:53,910 --> 01:29:56,041
- And the workers heard him
- Kkh!

1264
01:29:56,042 --> 01:29:58,435
- If it's true what they say
- Huh!

1265
01:29:58,436 --> 01:30:00,437
- With their hammer swinging
- Kkh!

1266
01:30:00,438 --> 01:30:02,613
-What's the purpose of a man?
-Huh!

1267
01:30:02,614 --> 01:30:04,572
- And they quit their working
- Kkh!

1268
01:30:04,573 --> 01:30:06,791
Just to turn his eyes away

1269
01:30:06,792 --> 01:30:08,967
- When they heard him singing
- Kkh

1270
01:30:08,968 --> 01:30:11,187
Just to throw up Both his hands

1271
01:30:11,188 --> 01:30:13,232
No hammer swinging

1272
01:30:13,233 --> 01:30:15,060
What's the use Of his backbone?

1273
01:30:15,061 --> 01:30:17,541
No pickax ring

1274
01:30:17,542 --> 01:30:19,369
If he never stands upright

1275
01:30:19,370 --> 01:30:21,719
And they stood and listened

1276
01:30:21,720 --> 01:30:24,026
If he turns his back On everyone

1277
01:30:24,027 --> 01:30:26,245
To the poor boy sing

1278
01:30:26,246 --> 01:30:28,422
That he could have Stood beside

1279
01:30:28,423 --> 01:30:31,338
If it's true what they say

1280
01:30:33,123 --> 01:30:37,519
I'll be on my way

1281
01:30:39,608 --> 01:30:43,132
But who are they to say

1282
01:30:43,133 --> 01:30:44,917
What the truth is anyway?

1283
01:30:46,441 --> 01:30:48,703
Ask the ones Who tell the lies

1284
01:30:48,704 --> 01:30:50,226
Ahh

1285
01:30:50,227 --> 01:30:52,621
Are the solemnest to swear

1286
01:30:54,840 --> 01:30:57,146
And the ones Who load the dice

1287
01:30:57,147 --> 01:30:58,452
Hmm

1288
01:30:58,453 --> 01:31:01,456
Always say the toss is fair

1289
01:31:02,935 --> 01:31:05,371
And the ones Who deal the cards

1290
01:31:05,372 --> 01:31:06,851
Deal the cards

1291
01:31:06,852 --> 01:31:08,897
Are the ones Who take the tricks

1292
01:31:08,898 --> 01:31:10,552
Ahh

1293
01:31:11,204 --> 01:31:13,902
With their hands
Over their hearts

1294
01:31:13,903 --> 01:31:15,207
Mmmm

1295
01:31:15,208 --> 01:31:19,473
While we play the game they fix

1296
01:31:19,474 --> 01:31:21,475
And the ones Who speak the word

1297
01:31:21,476 --> 01:31:23,215
Speak the word

1298
01:31:23,216 --> 01:31:26,001
Always say it is the last

1299
01:31:26,002 --> 01:31:27,524
Mmmm

1300
01:31:27,525 --> 01:31:30,746
And no answer Will be heard

1301
01:31:31,964 --> 01:31:35,010
To the question no one asks

1302
01:31:35,011 --> 01:31:36,926
So I'm asking if it's true!

1303
01:31:39,276 --> 01:31:41,146
I'm asking me and you

1304
01:31:41,147 --> 01:31:43,148
And you And you

1305
01:31:43,149 --> 01:31:45,281
I believe our answer matters

1306
01:31:45,282 --> 01:31:47,239
More than anything they say

1307
01:31:47,240 --> 01:31:49,285
We stand and listen

1308
01:31:49,286 --> 01:31:51,461
We stand

1309
01:31:51,462 --> 01:31:53,419
I believe if there is
Still a will

1310
01:31:53,420 --> 01:31:55,421
Then there is still a way

1311
01:31:55,422 --> 01:31:57,641
We're standing with him

1312
01:31:57,642 --> 01:31:59,687
I believe there is a way

1313
01:31:59,688 --> 01:32:03,691
I believe in us together
More than anyone alone

1314
01:32:03,692 --> 01:32:05,823
We're standing near him

1315
01:32:05,824 --> 01:32:07,999
Near him

1316
01:32:08,000 --> 01:32:10,001
I believe that with each other

1317
01:32:10,002 --> 01:32:12,003
We are stronger than we know

1318
01:32:12,004 --> 01:32:13,614
We hear him

